        "original_id": "b3bf1fbe-7f30-580d-a6c8-1e5fcc173563",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin Woo, Epic Mazur, Park Jimin, Jae, Eazy-E, Bilal Bashir\n- Organizations: XING Entertainment, Ruthless Records, Relativity Records\n- Products: Future Profits, \"Butterfly\"\n- Projects: After School Club, Crazy Town\n- Places: California, South Korea\n- Roles: singer, actor, television host, vocalist, rapper, record producer\n\nFacts:\n- Future Profits was released on November 16, 1993 for Ruthless Records and Relativity Records.\n- Future Profits was produced by Eazy-E, Epic Mazur, and Bilal Bashir.\n- Epic Mazur was born as Bret Hadley Mazur on August 31, 1970.\n- Epic Mazur is an American vocalist, rapper, and record producer.\n- Epic Mazur is a founder and frontman of Crazy Town, which is known for the hit song \"Butterfly.\"\n- Kevin Woo was born as Christopher Thomas Woo on November 25, 1991.\n- Kevin Woo is an American singer, actor, and television host based in South Korea.\n- Kevin Woo was born and raised in California.\n- Kevin Woo was discovered by XING Entertainment at age fifteen and then moved to South Korea.\n- After School Club is a South Korean internet-based live-music request television talk show.\n- After School Club is often shortened to ASC.\n- After School Club is co-hosted by Kevin Woo, Park Jimin, and Jae.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
